e Light Laws (2026 Guide)\",\n  \t\"description\": \"75 Pa.C.S. 4571 and 4572 plus the 67 Pa. Code Ch. 173 specs: flash rate limits, SAE color standards and the $500 penalty. Reviewed August 2026.\",\n  \t\"isPartOf\": {\n    \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/#website\"\n  \t},\n  \t\"breadcrumb\": {\n    \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/blogs/informative/pennsylvania-emergency-vehicle-light-laws#breadcrumb\"\n  \t},\n  \t\"lastReviewed\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \t\"reviewedBy\": {\n    \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/#organization\"\n  \t},\n  \t\"inLanguage\": \"en-US\"\n\t},\n\t{\n  \t\"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\",\n  \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/blogs/informative/pennsylvania-emergency-vehicle-light-laws#breadcrumb\",\n  \t\"itemListElement\": [\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"ListItem\",\n      \t\"position\": 1,\n      \t\"name\": \"Home\",\n      \t\"item\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/\"\n    \t},\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"ListItem\",\n      \t\"position\": 2,\n      \t\"name\": \"Informative Blogs\",\n      \t\"item\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/blogs/informative\"\n    \t},\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"ListItem\",\n      \t\"position\": 3,\n      \t\"name\": \"Pennsylvania Emergency Vehicle Light Laws\"\n    \t}\n  \t]\n\t},\n\t{\n  \t\"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\n  \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/blogs/informative/pennsylvania-emergency-vehicle-light-laws#faq\",\n  \t\"mainEntity\": [\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \t\"name\": \"What is the legal flash rate for emergency lights in Pennsylvania?\",\n      \t\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \t\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \t\"text\": \"67 Pa. Code § 173.3 requires a flash rate between 60 and 260 flashes per minute when observed from a fixed position.\"\n      \t}\n    \t},\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \t\"name\": \"Can Pennsylvania fire police use red and blue lights?\",\n      \t\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \t\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \t\"text\": \"Fire police vehicles are among the classes listed in 75 Pa.C.S. § 4571(b) that may display combination red and blue lights. PennDOT has stated that privately owned vehicles of fire police officers are not emergency vehicles and fall under section 4572 instead.\"\n      \t}\n    \t},\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \t\"name\": \"What is the penalty for illegal emergency lights in Pennsylvania?\",\n      \t\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \t\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \t\"text\": \"Under 75 Pa.C.S. § 4571(e), unauthorized use is a summary offense punishable by a fine of not less than $500 and not more than $1,000.\"\n      \t}\n    \t},\n    \t{\n      \t\"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \t\"name\": \"What colors are legal for flashing lights in Pennsylvania?\",\n      \t\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n        \t\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n        \t\"text\": \"67 Pa. Code § 173.3 permits white, clear, red, blue, amber or yellow for flashing or revolving lights, subject to the exception in subsection (a.1), and requires the lights to meet SAE J578d chromaticity coordinates or a subsequent SAE standard.\"\n      \t}\n    \t}\n  \t]\n\t},\n\t{\n  \t\"@type\": \"Organization\",\n  \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/#organization\",\n  \t\"name\": \"Strobes N' More\",\n  \t\"url\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/\",\n  \t\"telephone\": \"+1-401-454-4487\",\n  \t\"email\": \"sales@strobesnmore.com\",\n  \t\"address\": {\n    \t\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\n    \t\"streetAddress\": \"81 Tom Harvey Road\",\n    \t\"addressLocality\": \"Westerly\",\n    \t\"addressRegion\": \"RI\",\n    \t\"postalCode\": \"02891\",\n    \t\"addressCountry\": \"US\"\n  \t}\n\t},\n\t{\n  \t\"@type\": \"WebSite\",\n  \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/#website\",\n  \t\"url\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/\",\n  \t\"name\": \"Strobes N' More\",\n  \t\"publisher\": {\n    \t\"@id\": \"https://strobesnmore.com/#organization\"\n  \t}\n\t}\n  ]\n}\n</script>"
